course: dictionary
lesson: 14613
title: Slang and the dropped g
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Poppin' is slang, a casual way of talking. It is a spoken form of popping, and the apostrophe at the end shows that the g has been dropped. You will often hear it in everyday talk, in songs and in stories.
explain: In slang, poppin' can mean exciting and full of life: «The party is poppin'!» It can also mean that something looks bright and stands out: «Those red shoes are poppin'.» Read the words around it to see which meaning fits.
explain: You may also hear «What's poppin'?» as a greeting. It means «What's happening? How are you?» Ask yourself: is the word describing a place or a thing, or is someone saying hello? The context tells you.
fact: Poppin' is slang, so it is informal. You would not usually use it in a school essay.
fact: The apostrophe at the end shows a dropped g: poppin' is a spoken way of writing popping.
fact: «The party is poppin'» means the party is exciting, lively and full of people.
fact: «Those colours are poppin'» means they look bright and stand out.
fact: «What's poppin'?» is a greeting that means «What's happening? How are you?»
exercise: «The party is poppin'!» What does poppin' mean here? | Empty and quiet | Broken and sad | Very cold | *Exciting and full of fun
exercise: «Those yellow flowers are poppin' against the green grass.» What does poppin' mean here? | Falling over | Going to sleep | Hiding quietly | *Looking bright and standing out
exercise: Sam says «What's poppin'?» to his friend at the gate. What is he doing? | *Saying hello and asking how she is | Asking for a bottle of pop | Telling her to be quiet | Counting to ten
test: Which word is the spoken, dropped-g form of popping? | popular | *poppin' | pulling | popcorn
test: In «What's poppin'?» the apostrophe shows what? | A question mark | A full stop at the end | *A dropped letter g | A missing letter s
exam: Which sentence uses poppin' as a greeting? | «Please put the bread in the oven.» | «Where is your bag, Ava?» | «The shop is closed today.» | *«What's poppin', Ava?»
